Let $p\in S$ be a preperiodic point. By the properties of the Markov accesses associated with points in $S$, the corresponding branch of the Markov map $f_G$ can be extended holomorphically  to a sufficiently small neighborhood $V_p$ of $p$.

	By composing some conformal homeomorphisms $\gamma$ and $\eta$ of the unit ball $\mathbb{B}^{3}$, we can normalize $f$ by $F\left ( \xi \right )= \eta \circ f\circ \zeta ^{-1} \left ( \xi \right )$ with $F(0)=0.$ Let $k\geq 1$ be the order of the zero of $F$ at $0$. Taylor expansion of $F$ at $0$ as $$F\left ( \xi \right )= b_{k} \xi^{k} +O\left ( \xi^{k+1}  \right )  ,$$ where $b_{k}=F^{(k)}(0)/k!.$
	Observe that $$F^{'} \left ( \xi \right )= kb_{k}\xi^{k-1} +O\left ( \xi^{k}  \right ).$$
	For sufficiently small $\left | \xi \right |$ ,we have  $\left | F\left ( \xi \right )  \right |\sim \left | \xi \right |^{k}   $ and $\left | F^{'} \left ( \xi \right )  \right |\sim \left | \xi \right |^{k-1},$ and
	\begin{align}
		\frac{\left | F^{'} \left ( \xi \right )  \right |\left | \xi \right | }{\left | F\left ( \xi \right )  \right | }\sim 1 .\end{align}
	Hence, for sufficiently small $\left | \xi \right |,$
	\begin{align}\left | F^{'}\left ( \xi \right )   \right | \ge C \frac{\left | F\left ( \xi \right )  \right | }{\left | \xi \right | }, \end{align} where $C$ is a positive constant.

	Let $f\left ( p \right ) =q.$ Note that the spherical distance  $\left | z- p \right | _{\sigma }$ is equivalent to the Euclidean distance $ \left | \xi -0\right | $ in a  sufficiently small coordinate neighborhood of $p$,  we have that \begin{align}\left | f\left ( z \right ) - q \right | _{\sigma }\sim \left | F\left ( \xi  \right )   \right |\end{align}
	and the spherical derivative is equivalent to the local coordinate derivative \begin{align}
		\left | f^{'}\left ( z \right )   \right | _{\sigma } \sim \left | F^{'}\left ( \xi  \right )   \right | .
	\end{align}
	Furthermore, for any $z\in V_{p} \setminus \left \{ p \right \} ,$  we can find a positive constant $C$ such that
	\begin{align}\left | f^{'}\left ( z \right )   \right | _{\sigma } \ge C \frac{\left | f\left ( z \right ) - q \right |_{\sigma }  }{\left |z-p \right |_{\sigma }  } .\end{align}

	In conclusion, for any point $p\in S $, by(3.6-3.10), there exists a neighbourhood $V_{p}$ such that for all $z\in V_{p} \setminus \left \{ p \right \} ,$ we have $$A(V_{p})= \inf_{ z\in V_{p}} \frac{\left | f^{'} \left ( z \right )  \right | _{\sigma }  \, |z-p|_{\sigma}}{|f(z)-f  (p)|_{\sigma}} \geq C> 0.$$
